buck@pool.info.sunyit.edu (Jesse Buckley) writes:

>I'd like to see a mail daemon.  How can I get him to show up.

In my experience, the mail daemon only appears on *IX systems when the
following conditions are met: a) the option is enabled at compile-time,
and b) you receive mail from some source.  You can't kill this daemon -
it just gives you a scroll of mail and then disappears.  When you read
that scroll, nethack executes whatever mail program it was told (at
compile time) to use.
